<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill drops to 10.07 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill drops to 10.07 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it set a cut-off price of 97.55 rupees at the five billion rupee weekly auction of 91-day treasury bills, against 97.54 at the previous auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield worked out to 10.07 percent, down from 10.11 percent at the previous auction.</p>
<p>				  Bids received	Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive			   28		     6,756.4</p>
<p>Non-competitive			3		     3,000.0</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   31		     9,756.4</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>				   Bids allotted     Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive (6 partial)	   17		   3,039.625</p>
<p>Non-competitive (all partial)    3		   1,960.375</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   20		   5,000.000</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Devolvement : Reserve Bank of India			nil</p>
<p>		  Primary dealers				nil</p>
<p>Weighted average price - 97.56 rupees.</p>
